PRISM Models and compatibles

A guide to the often confusing world of early 802.11 network adapters. 
:Besides, they are all &quot;functionally equivalent.&quot; YEAH! RIGHT!

Note on FCC ID and ODM/OEM info:
FCC ID listed has been verified via «FCC OET Database»«FCC OET Database» . ODM/OEM info is often printed on the circuit board or included in the FCC data. ODM/OEM data can not be 100% verified. It would not be unusual to find more than one ODM/OEM per product.
NOTE: It may be illegal to use cards marked with an invalid FCC ID in the US.
High power cards (&gt;100mW) are intended for OEM use and the FCC requires that these cards MUST NOT work in Laptop PCs.
There are hundreds of &quot;branded&quot; PRISM models. This list covers only the fraction that have been verified as being PRISM based or often confused with similar PRISM models. &quot;Everybody&quot; made a PRISM WLAN adapter at one time or another:) 
Appearance on this list DOES NOT imply that the NetBSD wi(4) driver directly supports the adapter. Some adjustments may be necessary.

