1. (LH) Some cards use the same Manufacturer and Product ID as Lucent for their Hermes based cards. Oops!
2. These cards are listed as using a Symbol MAC chip, however the hardware pictures show a Harris HFA3841 
:PRISM II MAC on the LA4121 and an Intersil ISL3873 PRISM 2.5 MAC on the LA4131.
3. The PRISM chipset was designed to be a superset of the Lucent Hermes. These Lucent Hermes based cards 
:will also work with the «wi(4)»«wi(4)» driver.
4. PRISM 3 cards marked in yellow are known to require firmware download -- the cards do not include firmware in flash. 
:The only PRISM 3 model known to work with NetBSD is the BroMax WE300 / Linksys WPC11 Ver. 3.
5. These nearly identical cards are incompatible with PRISM drivers.
a) ADMtek ADM8211 is supported on CardBus and PCI systems by the NetBSD «atw(4)»«atw(4)» driver. 
:ADMtek says that the ADM8211 cannot act as an access point.
b)RealTek RTL8180L is supported on CardBus and PCI systems by the NetBSD «rtw(4)»«rtw(4)» driver.
6. These nearly identical cards currently have no open source drivers.
a) Atmel chipset is currently unsupported.
b) Broadcom BCM4307 is currently unsupported.
c) InproComm IPN2120 is currently unsupported.
d) TI ACX100 is currently unsupported.

